{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Howzit, I'm just going to do your readings quickly before the doctor calls you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, shame, we sat twenty minutes at that robot by the mall. Load shedding again, the lights were dead.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He wanted to turn around and go home, hey. I told him no.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (NURSE): Blood pressure is one oh nine over seventy-seven. Temperature is thirty-eight point three.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Pulse I first saw as ninety-two. Ag, wrong column, sorry. It's seventy-six. Last time in March you were sixty-eight, and your last pressure was one-forty.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): One-forty, ja, that sounds like the old me. I've been walking more. The bakkie's been in the garage so I walk to the shop.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (NURSE): Mm. I'll leave the file here. My sister went through this night-time weeing thing too, when her little one was still a baby, she was finished.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (DOCTOR): Morning. Take a seat. What's the main trouble today?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): It's the getting up at night to wee, three times, sometimes four, and the stream is weak and then it dribbles afterwards. Um, did you catch the Springboks? Ag, never mind.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (DOCTOR): Leave the rugby. The getting up, the weak stream, the dribbling. How long has that been going on?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Err. Last winter, or the one before. I honestly can't pin it. It just sort of crept in.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'm the one who hears him. Every night, up and down, and there's drips on the tiles.",
  "[SEG0013] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any blood in the urine?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No blood. It's just ordinary wee.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any burning when you pass water, or pain in the lower tummy?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No burning. No pain. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (DOCTOR): What are you drinking in the evenings?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Tea. Two cups, sometimes three, Five Roses, after supper, while the news is on. She makes it strong. Well, you do, ja.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I do. He won't drink rooibos, says it tastes like grass.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (DOCTOR): Ok so, thinking it through. The prostate sits round the water pipe, and when it enlarges it squeezes the pipe. That's why the stream is thin and you dribble at the end, and the bladder doesn't empty properly, so you're up at night.",
  "[SEG0021] person_4 (DOCTOR): I was going to start you on tamsolosin, zero point four milligrams at night. It relaxes that muscle.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His pressure looked low just now, and last week he went all woozy standing up off the couch.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, light in the head, just a second or two. Not every day. I sat down and it passed.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Right, one oh nine over seventy-seven and those dizzy spells, tamsolosin can drop the pressure further. I'm changing my mind, I won't start it today.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): So no tablet? I already told my neighbour at the braai I was getting a pill. Eish.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (DOCTOR): No tablet today. What I will do is book a PSA blood test and a urine test for this week. The temperature is thirty-eight point three, a bit warm, so I don't want to miss a urine infection.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (DOCTOR): My working impression is an enlarged prostate, benign, but that's provisional. I also can't rule out a urine infection until the tests are back.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): PSA, that's the one they talk about at the chemist, ja? My cousin's dog, no, my cousin, had a high one, but I don't know the story properly.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (DOCTOR): Ja. Don't compare with braai talk. Cut the tea after supper, less fluid in the evening. That's your job.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'll pack the Five Roses away after six. He'll moan.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, man. A small cup? We'll see. The garden's been dry anyway, I've been... uh, sorry, that's not your problem.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): Come back in three weeks and we'll go through the results. If you get feverish or you can't pass water at all, don't wait, come in sooner.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks, ja. If the bakkie's fixed I'll drive. Otherwise she brings me.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): Sister, the forms for the PSA and the urine, please.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (NURSE): I'll print them just now and book both for this week at the desk.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Lekker. Thanks, hey. Sorry about the rugby tangent.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (DOCTOR): You're fine. See you in three weeks."
 ],
